WEBVTT

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.270
We will reach the Desert Area shortly.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.870
If you'd like, have a look 
through the window above you.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.830
Above us?

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.380
What is this? You can climb up?

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.690
Wow!

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.180
Look at all that sand.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.850
Due to the extremely small amount 
of precipitation in the Desert Area,

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:43.890
there is much sand and rock, 
but very little vegetation.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.970
There are actually several kinds of deserts.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:52.940
Sandy deserts such as this one 
are actually relatively rare.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.700
Is this road safe?

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:05.040
The library lies just beyond the Desert Area.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.340
Leave the driving to me.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:12.700
Huh?

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:48.520
Lucky-san?

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:50.700
There is a sandstorm ahead.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:55.330
Sandstorms are not unusual in the desert,

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:58.280
but inhaling sand is bad for your health.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.280
Huh?

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.750
We will take a detour.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.380
Huh?

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.040
Boss!

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.800
Lucky-san!

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.410
What do we do? Should we push it?

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:20.660
On it!

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:32.730
Whoa!

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.650
The storm's coming closer!

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:54.740
Serval-chan!

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:04.690
Looks like we're safe now. That was scary!

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:07.430
Thank you for your help. What's your name?

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:13.480
Order: Carnivora
Family: Felidae
Genus: Felis

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:09.780
I'm Sand Cat.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:12.860
Wow, you're just as cute as the rumors say!

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.660
Your voice is totally adorable, too!

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:22.060
You're just as clumsy as the 
rumors say you are, too, Serval.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:25.570
Aw, hey! That wasn't my fault earlier!

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:29.240
What were you doing there, Sand Cat-san?

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:32.580
Since that sandstorm was so big,

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.830
I got curious and went to check it out.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.540
Then I got swept away,

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.810
and the next thing I knew, I was here.

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:39.720
Really?!

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.350
That was dangerous!

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:45.350
When something makes me curious, 
I can't stop myself from—

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.560
Wow...

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:56.220
This is incredible. What is it?

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:59.400
This is called a "bus."

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.510
We found it in pieces in the Jungle.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.660
It was a lot of work.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:10.410
We took this "battery" thing up a really 
tall cliff, all the way to a café, and...

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.830
I see.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.410
Come on, show a little more interest!

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.150
Huh? What is that?

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.340
Huh? Do you mean this?

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.300
I thought it was an ear at first. It's pretty!

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:27.830
Oh, that's the decoration on my hat.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:29.250
Okay.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:30.890
She already lost interest!

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:34.870
So this is what Sand Cat is like, huh?

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:40.860
It's said that the sand cat's body can 
both heat and cool itself easily.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:45.270
This may have influenced her 
transformation into a Friend.

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:48.410
Wow, Boss can talk!

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:50.700
But...

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:53.200
I guess it's not that big a deal.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.220
She cools off too fast!

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:57.750
She's a very unique Friend, huh?

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:03.250
We should be safe from 
the storm at this distance.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.750
This is the desert, too?

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:10.720
It feels completely different.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:19.480
Most deserts are covered in rock, like this.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:22.150
There are also white deserts

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:25.400
and deserts covered in pebbles.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:29.220
Where are you all going?

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:30.720
To the library!

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.910
Boss says this is a fast way to get there.

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:34.970
Shall we move on?

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:38.290
Boss is more fun when he talks.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:41.340
But he won't say anything 
when Kaban-chan isn't around.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.950
Maybe he just doesn't like you, Serval?

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.090
That's not it!

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:49.340
It's so hot here.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:53.200
The temperature range in 
the Desert Area is extreme.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:57.220
It is not unusual for the temperature 
to exceed 100 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:59.270
Wow!

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:01.600
It sounds like it'd be hard to live there.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:05.500
This is why there are many desert animals

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:10.900
that evolved to be tolerant of the 
heat and not easily dehydrated.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:16.330
This bus is great for beating the heat. 
It's like we're running through the shade.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.300
Hot! Hot!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.300
Boss, it's hot!

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.920
The floor is burning up! Hot!

00:07:27.390 --> 00:07:31.350
Really? It feels fine to me.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.670
Huh?

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:37.140
The bottoms of the sand cat's 
paws are covered in thick fur,

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:40.080
so hot sand doesn't bother them.

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:42.370
Oh, that explains it.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:48.030
Boss, can we go someplace cool? 
We're going to dry up.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:51.240
Would you like to visit my home, then?

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.240
Your home?

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:05.540
Much better!

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:09.990
This is my home.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:15.900
I usually stay here in the 
daytime and go out at night.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:19.390
Today I got to see so many 
unusual things that I got bored.

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:20.970
My curiosity is sated.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:22.980
Sounds like a fun life.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:29.000
Would you like to eat some Japari buns?

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.320
Yay!

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:33.680
What should we do next?

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:35.850
Maybe move during the night?

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:38.660
Nighttime in the desert is very cold.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:40.950
That doesn't sound so great, either.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.960
Would you like to go through 
the hole further in?

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:45.630
A hole?

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:52.700
This would be the bypass.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:56.040
You can go this way to get to the library, too.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:59.000
But the bus can't get through here.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.730
Shall I dig it out?

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:01.830
Huh?

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:13.820
You're great, Sand Cat!

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.200
It's pitch dark.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:25.120
Boss, can we go through here?

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.800
Shall we?

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.030
What a mysterious road.

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:40.850
I wonder where it leads.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:43.020
My curiosity is sated.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:44.810
Already?!

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:48.520
That's it for me today.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:55.690
I don't get bored with you all around. 
Let's play again sometime.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.210
Sure.

00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:58.450
We'd be happy to!

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:06.710
Her yawns were contagious.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:09.330
Well, you are both nocturnal.

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:12.420
Look, there's something up ahead!

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:18.930
What is this place?

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:23.930
It looks like you can walk inside.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.690
Wanna check it out?

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:31.780
They have longer fur that 
covers the paws of their feet

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:57.110
Big Cat Rescue, Lauren-oneesan (America)

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:34.530
because they walk on the hot sand

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:38.450
and because of the high-temperature 
terrain that they move on.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:44.730
Those hairs help to protect their 
paws from getting burnt.

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:47.730
Sand cats are prolific diggers.

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:51.310
Many cats tend to be climbers or jumpers,

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:57.380
but for sand cats, digging is necessary 
to help the cat dig out burrows.

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:04.930
What is this place?

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.680
Yeah, what is it?

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.390
It looks like it goes deeper.

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:20.170
Huh?!

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:28.030
What's going on?

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:39.550
Wh-Wh-Wh-Who are you?!

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:48.970
<i>Welcome to the Underground Labyrinth! 
Can you make it to the exit in one piece?</i>

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:55.420
You closed it?! You jerks!

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:57.370
Huh?! S-Sorry!

00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:59.360
Also, who are you?

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.470
Use your eyes! I'm Tsuchinoko!

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:03.910
Cryptid

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:03.910
But I can't see you!

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:08.120
What's going on? Where are we?

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.330
Darn it... And after I 
propped that door open

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:15.920
because it's hard to get out 
of here when it's closed...

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:18.230
Why won't you come out?

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:20.460
Because this calms me!

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:23.680
Whatever. I'll try somewhere else.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:26.090
You guys do what it says and go to the exit, too.

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:28.260
Which way's the exit?

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:31.270
I don't know! I'm gonna look for it, too.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:35.190
Watch out for Ceruleans.

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:36.110
Huh?!

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:41.820
Um... Can't we go together?

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:43.860
What?!

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:57.230
What do you think you're doing?! 
These are priceless ruins!

00:12:57.230 --> 00:12:59.140
I-I'm sorry!

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:03.920
Um... May we go with you?

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:06.890
Curses...

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:09.930
Follow me!

00:13:10.610 --> 00:13:12.120
Yay...

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:20.850
What is this place?

00:13:20.850 --> 00:13:24.150
The ruins of a place built long ago.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.990
Ruins?

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:30.660
You're moving right along. 
Do you know where the exit is?

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:35.040
I can smell it. The scent of the air outside.

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:37.300
That's amazing!

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:38.630
Wow!

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:41.290
Is your nose just for show?!

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:45.050
Well, I can't tell which scent is from outside.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.160
It's a fork in the path.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:52.810
Which way now?

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:57.550
The exit is that way... 
but there are Ceruleans.

00:13:57.550 --> 00:13:59.230
We'll go the other way!

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:00.850
Wow!

00:14:00.850 --> 00:14:03.060
How can you tell?

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:04.470
My pit organ.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:10.240
I think that's what it's called... 
It lets me see infrared light.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.860
Nothing gets past me.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:21.260
This place is huge! I wonder what it's for.

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:23.580
I-I'm researching that.

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:25.790
Huh?

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.540
We can't go through here?

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:31.180
It was probably a way out in the past,

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:34.630
but not anymore, with the lava plugging it up.

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:36.270
What's "lava"?

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:39.430
Tch! Ask at the library!

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:47.220
They're here.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:58.730
Don't get too close. There are a lot of them.

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:00.040
No worries!

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:05.380
There's a wall between us and them. 
Besides, I can beat them with my claws!

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:09.170
Behind you!

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:19.100
What's wrong with you?!

00:15:19.610 --> 00:15:21.590
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:26.400
What do we do, Kaban-chan?!

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:31.600
Stay on the right side of 
the bridge! The right side!

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:32.260
Huh?!

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:32.700
Got it!

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:42.670
Huh?! It's a dead end!

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.590
Oh, no! They're here!

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:02.220
If we had fallen... If we had fallen, we'd be...

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:13.700
What is it, Tsuchinoko?

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:16.490
What's that?

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:19.300
This is a Japari coin!

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:21.110
It was once used as currency at the park.

00:16:21.110 --> 00:16:25.320
Oh, currency was something 
you could exchange for things,

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:27.380
like modern Japari buns, and—

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.770
What's your problem?!

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:36.570
We wanna hear!

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:41.270
Come on, we're heading for the exit.

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.060
That way!

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:47.860
We just came through that way!

00:16:48.210 --> 00:16:50.600
I think that one's small enough to fight off.

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:52.280
Then you go fight it.

00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:01.700
Is that the exit? I can see light!

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:04.310
This is...

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:05.880
Here, too?

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:09.260
Can't get through here...

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:13.090
Meow!

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:15.300
Hi-yah!

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:17.490
It'd be tough to dig through, too.

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:19.530
Isn't there another exit?

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:22.010
I can only smell the outside from here.

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:25.660
What? Then we're stuck in here?!

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:28.860
Hey, I don't mind staying here a while longer.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:30.220
What?!

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.860
I find the darkness calming.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:35.390
I don't wanna stay!

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:37.610
Might be more interesting 
artifacts to find, too.

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:39.490
No! No!

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:42.980
Excuse me... I think something's over here.

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:45.000
Really?

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:48.530
Yes. I saw this symbol earlier, too.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:56.330
I knew it.

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:02.310
Just... what kind of animal are you?

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.810
I don't know yet.

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:30.170
An incredible find!

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:37.010
I was right! This place was 
built for entertainment!

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:39.170
It's probably not—

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:43.010
Uh-huh? Uh-huh?

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:47.880
A-Ahem. It's probably not on the map

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:52.110
because the lava became a problem 
before it was formally opened.

00:18:58.010 --> 00:18:58.740
Boss!

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:05.560
How was it? Because the attraction began, 
I moved to the exit to pick you up.

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:10.970
Lucky Beast spoke?!

00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:14.590
Yeah! But he won't talk to me...

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.720
Well, that's normal.

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:20.430
Wait, could you be...

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:31.980
Ahem! Our new attraction, the 
Underground Labyrinth, is now open!

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:34.390
It's that again!

00:19:34.390 --> 00:19:35.260
Huh?

00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:40.120
Boss made that voice earlier, 
too, while you were asleep.

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:46.700
This giant attraction is a maze where you 
can play together with animals and Friends.

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:49.460
We hope you'll enjoy it.

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:54.710
Goodbye, and we look forward 
to meeting you all!

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:06.420
Bye, Tsuchinoko!

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:15.360
Today was a good day. Come back 
sometime, if you get the chance.

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:16.840
Okay!

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:18.860
Are you being shy?

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:21.050
<i>You</i> don't need to!

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:22.780
That's mean!

00:20:23.430 --> 00:20:24.790
The bus is now departing.

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:36.980
So she wasn't annihilated, huh?

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:42.580
Well, that was a curious place!

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:43.970
Yup!

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:25.580
They're generally about 30 to 40 centimeters 
long and narrower at the neck,

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:49.760
Tsuchinoko Museum, Yasue-oniisan (Gifu)

00:22:25.580 --> 00:22:27.420
with a tiny tail and no limbs.

00:22:27.420 --> 00:22:31.360
People say that they scrunch up 
like inchworms and then jump,

00:22:31.360 --> 00:22:34.480
and tumble down from the mountains and so on.

00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:37.710
Younger people doubt their existence,

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:39.670
but personally, I think they're real.

00:22:39.670 --> 00:22:43.980
When I was a child, old folks would say that 
the back hills were crawling with them,

00:22:43.980 --> 00:22:49.780
and it was more than just one or 
two people, so I think it's true.

00:22:55.970 --> 00:22:59.060
You've gotta be careful, Raccoon-san.

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:03.390
If not for this contraption...

00:23:04.470 --> 00:23:05.320
Who's that?

00:23:05.580 --> 00:23:08.070
Kaban-chan made it.

00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:13.680
It saved me. I owe my life to this Kaban-san!

00:23:13.680 --> 00:23:15.630
So what are you in such a hurry for?

00:23:16.050 --> 00:23:19.960
We're trying to catch up with someone 
who has something like this on her head.

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:22.500
Her? She went to that mountain, and—

00:23:23.480 --> 00:23:25.170
After her!

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:27.300
Uh, and then...

00:23:28.290 --> 00:23:30.630
Thanks for the tip.

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:33.990
Raccoon-san, don't be in such a rush.

00:23:34.870 --> 00:23:38.830
And then she came back and got on the bus...

00:23:41.800 --> 00:23:43.090
PPP Preview!

00:23:43.090 --> 00:23:46.110
This week, let's learn about prairie dogs.

00:23:46.110 --> 00:23:49.380
They're polygamous, 
and their families are close-knit.

00:23:49.380 --> 00:23:51.080
All the wives must get along well.

00:23:51.080 --> 00:23:52.500
There's no way!

00:23:52.500 --> 00:23:53.540
I'm not convinced.

00:23:53.540 --> 00:23:54.350
No way!

00:23:54.350 --> 00:23:54.840
Did something happen?

00:23:54.840 --> 00:23:56.410
Next time, "Lake Shore."
